From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:13:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] .16 Paper Execution: required-vs-optional symbol
 handling for full coin universe

Same pattern as .13/.14/.15: REQUIRED_SYMBOLS (BTC/ETH) remain the only
symbols whose absence or invalid position state can block the whole
paper-execution decision. Every other symbol .15 reports -- including one
.15 itself individually blocked -- gets its own execution decision
independently.

Specific changes:
- New position_state_errors(symbol, item, allow_blocked) helper factors
  out the original per-symbol validity check (valid position_state,
  position_exists must be False); called with allow_blocked=False for the
  required-symbol gate (preserving exact prior behavior/reason strings)
  and allow_blocked=True per optional symbol, since an optional symbol may
  legitimately arrive BLOCKED from .15's own optional-symbol handling.
- verify_upstream()'s per-symbol loop scoped to REQUIRED_SYMBOLS only.
- build_paper_execution()'s main loop iterates every symbol .15 reported
  (union with REQUIRED_SYMBOLS): required symbols keep the original
  ENTRY_CANDIDATE->PAPER_ORDER_INTENT / FLAT->NO_ORDER logic; optional
  symbols get the same plus BLOCKED handling, recorded in
  optional_symbols_blocked, without affecting the required pair.
- print_report() iterates actual decisions instead of a fixed BTC/ETH
  tuple, labeling each symbol REQUIRED/OPTIONAL.

live_execution_permitted remains hard-coded False regardless of any of
this -- a paper order intent still never implies a position exists.

Adds 10 contract tests, including optional-blocked-does-not-cascade and
an optional-symbol-position-exists-true test. Full suite (51 tests) green.

